#: ../pwntools/docs/source/config.rst:2
msgid ":mod:`pwnlib.config` --- Pwntools Configuration File"
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.config:1
msgid "Allows per-user and per-host configuration of Pwntools settings."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.config:3
msgid ""
"The list of configurable options includes all of the logging symbols and "
"colors, as well as all of the default values on the global context "
"object."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.config:7
msgid ""
"The configuration file is read from ``~/.pwn.conf``, "
"``$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/pwn.conf`` (``$XDG_CONFIG_HOME`` defaults to "
"``~/.config``, per XDG Base Directory Specification), and "
"``/etc/pwn.conf``."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.config:11
msgid ""
"The configuration file is only read in ``from pwn import *`` mode, and "
"not when used in library mode (``import pwnlib``).  To read the "
"configuration file in library mode, invoke :func:`.config.initialize`."
msgstr ""

#: of pwnlib.config:15
msgid ""
"The ``context`` section supports complex types, at least as far as is "
"supported by :func:`pwnlib.util.safeeval.expr`."
msgstr ""

